{% extends "decision.jinja" %}
{% block question %}Review the credit call on loan application {{ application }} against the underwriting policy in the context. Which policy was applied? Were income, assets, employment and credit verified before the credit call? Does the credit call follow the policy's thresholds for the figures on record? Does the credit call's record state the thresholds applied and the factors it rested on? Does it rest only on factors the policy names? If it is a decline, does it record its principal reasons? How many hard inquiries were made on the borrower's credit file? Which conditions did the policy require (a large deposit sourced, an employment gap explained), and was each cleared on documented evidence? How many times was the borrower asked to explain again what they had already explained at origination? Was the credit call made consistently with the policy? If the context holds no policy text, consistency cannot be verified: answer null.{% endblock %}
{% block shape %}{"policyApplied": "policy id or null", "verifiedBeforeCall": true, false or null, "callMatchesThresholds": true, false or null, "hardInquiries": number, "borrowerReexplained": number, "conditionsDocumented": true, false or null, "thresholdsRecorded": true, false or null, "onlyPolicyFactors": true, false or null, "declineReasons": true, false or null (null if not a decline), "consistent": true, false or null, "findings": ["one sentence per finding"]}{% endblock %}
